                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bf68e778-9c7d-3d3b-813a-0fa47e3dce29",
                        "entry_id": "3ee291f5-c7f9-3c90-8a9d-97b55f5372eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "пристрастие к щегольской одежде, к изысканным вещам и т. п."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9614457c-58e1-4591-959d-15c13fe7837e",
                                "sense_id": "bf68e778-9c7d-3d3b-813a-0fa47e3dce29",
                                "text": "Туалеты дам отличались изысканным щегольством."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2854d9cb-8672-4e51-90aa-fb8e23fafa6d",
                                "sense_id": "bf68e778-9c7d-3d3b-813a-0fa47e3dce29",
                                "text": "Подчиняясь своей страсти к щегольству, он в Москве купил у какого-то своего земляка венгерку с шнурами."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f4f86d01-6ddf-3b5e-b9fa-4f97d0660573",
                        "entry_id": "3ee291f5-c7f9-3c90-8a9d-97b55f5372eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "хвастовство, молодечество"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a1cafb6-0f49-4b17-8ff1-3b53ba641f7b",
                                "sense_id": "f4f86d01-6ddf-3b5e-b9fa-4f97d0660573",
                                "text": "Меховая шапка острая кверху, так широка и высока, что может покрывать лоб и щёки; кроме того, для щегольства и большего тепла надеваются налобники, наушники, наносники и набородники; особенно налобник, вышивается разноцветными шелками и золотом."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "61c3e0c1-3c9d-4d13-b1f1-b1a7aa471e51",
                                "sense_id": "f4f86d01-6ddf-3b5e-b9fa-4f97d0660573",
                                "text": "Кролика [жеребца] совсем не выводили барышникам, Любезного же выводили ради особого щегольства, и притом очень крупным барышникам, известным как любители и знатоки."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "61ab4381-19df-4015-ac9b-0fe9de09005b",
                                "sense_id": "f4f86d01-6ddf-3b5e-b9fa-4f97d0660573",
                                "text": "— Мне холодно, — сказала Таня. … Петя стал так торопливо снимать куртку, что в ней что-то треснуло. Оставшись в одной белой рубашке, он для щегольства ещё закатал рукава и раскрыл ворот."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d456e089-3ba0-4b5a-b8ac-fb134416bf8b",
                        "source_entry_id": "3ee291f5-c7f9-3c90-8a9d-97b55f5372eb",
                        "source_sense_description": "пристрастие к щегольской одежде, к изысканным вещам",
                        "target_lang_word": "panache",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "panache",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea909140-f948-3e93-bc94-96c9a4133bce",
                                        "entry_id": "f67cb7f2-df2a-3d98-8cf8-7feeeca51970",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ornamental plume on a helmet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f813732-a437-4db1-9931-a027ef7cc87b",
                                                "sense_id": "ea909140-f948-3e93-bc94-96c9a4133bce",
                                                "text": "I had taken the panache from my shako so that it might escape notice, but even with my fine overcoat I feared that sooner or later my uniform would betray me."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e306a5ac-d516-3789-a97d-3a38f83b846b",
                                        "entry_id": "f67cb7f2-df2a-3d98-8cf8-7feeeca51970",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Flamboyance, energetic style or action."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa99b338-379e-4eca-a156-1317b202c67e",
                                                "sense_id": "e306a5ac-d516-3789-a97d-3a38f83b846b",
                                                "text": "One old gentleman, who was in the habit of reading a Paris newspaper and knew things, chuckled gleefully to everybody that Alcée’s conduct was altogether chic, mais chic. That he had more panache than Boulanger. Well, perhaps he had."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43a9464e-b8d0-43b9-b6a8-32999da896fb",
                                                "sense_id": "e306a5ac-d516-3789-a97d-3a38f83b846b",
                                                "text": "Cyberpunk caters to the wish-fulfillment requirements of male teen-agers, but this is a job that can be done with varying degrees of panache, and there is currently no more accomplished caterer than William Gibson."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f07d797f-4820-4672-9124-2b0a46523339",
                                                "sense_id": "e306a5ac-d516-3789-a97d-3a38f83b846b",
                                                "text": "It was a tantalizing promise, delivered with Donald Trump’s trademark panache: As dealmaker in chief, he would quickly end world conflicts that had defied his predecessors and their nattily dressed legions of career diplomats."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "558eeaa0-fbe3-41e7-a898-ece9dd7790b2",
                                                "sense_id": "e306a5ac-d516-3789-a97d-3a38f83b846b",
                                                "text": "It takes serious chutzpah for an American to bring a film abour the French New Wave to Cannes but [Richard] Linklater pulls it off with considerable comic panache and affection."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d577d73a-7f5b-4f9a-bf37-6092635d45da",
                        "source_entry_id": "3ee291f5-c7f9-3c90-8a9d-97b55f5372eb",
                        "source_sense_description": "пристрастие к щегольской одежде, к изысканным вещам",
                        "target_lang_word": "foppery",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "foppery",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f5de862-2ed7-3833-8856-bab88442cd6a",
                                        "entry_id": "e85025e4-1703-3ea5-975b-bbabca019198",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The dress or actions of a fop."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35dced0c-bcae-44b4-8ff3-8c268e64439c",
                                                "sense_id": "2f5de862-2ed7-3833-8856-bab88442cd6a",
                                                "text": "And it is by their fopperies and their frivolities that we know that their sinister philosophy is sincere; in their lights and garlands and ribbons we read their indwelling despair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b46b155-bc7e-33f3-8d18-127bed6d901b",
                                        "entry_id": "e85025e4-1703-3ea5-975b-bbabca019198",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Stupidity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e8690c9-58b1-4e8e-b1ad-7e61defbbe55",
                                                "sense_id": "2b46b155-bc7e-33f3-8d18-127bed6d901b",
                                                "text": "This is the excellent foppery of the world, that, / when we are sick in fortune,–often the surfeit / of our own behavior,–we make guilty of our / disasters the sun, the moon, and the stars: as / if we were villains by necessity; fools by / heavenly compulsion […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "906b53c3-b5f9-4ffb-b5d6-bcc8e539f5e4",
                                                "sense_id": "2b46b155-bc7e-33f3-8d18-127bed6d901b",
                                                "text": "The energies of his mind led him to despise the fopperies of idolatry; and he found the Christians, in the most unfavourable situation, torn into innumerable parties, by the sectaries of Athanasius, Arius, Eutyches, Nestorius."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "535b09db-3c00-412e-8e62-1f39d205ccf3",
                                                "sense_id": "2b46b155-bc7e-33f3-8d18-127bed6d901b",
                                                "text": "Still, still the secret presses;\nThe nearing clouds draw down;\nThe crimson morning flames into\nThe fopperies of the town."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "02da3415-3ccc-4e7d-b5b4-1aa5fc813642",
                        "source_entry_id": "3ee291f5-c7f9-3c90-8a9d-97b55f5372eb",
